    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">The Meaning of Ballynorsken</span>
      <h2>The Village of the Northern Lights</h2>
      <p>Ballynorsken is a name born from two worlds. "Bally" comes from the Irish word "Baile," meaning "the village of" or "the town of" — a word found throughout Ireland's place names. "Norsken" is inspired by the Swedish word for "the Norse ones," a natural nod to where we found belonging and a deep sense of connection.</p>
      <p>Together, Ballynorsken means <em>the Village of the Northern Lights</em> — a place where a name is our promise, and every experience is rooted in authenticity.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">A Place Between Two Worlds</span>
      <p class="mb-sm"><strong>Irish Roots.</strong> From the green hills of Ireland comes our heritage of warmth, storytelling and a deep connection to land and community.</p>
      <p><strong>Nordic Home.</strong> In the far north of Sweden, we found our wilderness — the forests, mountains, clear skies and the Northern Lights that inspired our name.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-cream">
  <div class="wrap content-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Our Story</span>
      <h2>A dream rooted in the North</h2>
      <p>Ballynorsken was born from a deep love for the Nordic wilderness, our dogs and the land. The journey began with Norwegian Elk Hounds and a passion for tradition and the bond between dog and human — and from that foundation, our dream expanded to everything that embodies the spirit of the north: cabins, culture, training and unforgettable adventures. This is our story. This is our life. This is Ballynorsken.</p>
      <p><strong>Our Heritage.</strong> For generations, these dogs have worked alongside people in forests and mountains — their courage, intelligence and endurance handed down. We're honoured to continue that tradition and preserve it for the breed's future.</p>
      <p><strong>Our Home.</strong> We're in the far north of Sweden — deep forests, clear lakes and long winters — between Överkalix and Kalix in Norrbotten. This is where we raise our dogs, build our cabins, welcome guests and live our everyday life. It shapes everything we do.</p>
      <p>At the heart of it stands Klippets Tirhild — Elsa — whose image has become the visual ambassador for Ballynorsken.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame"><img src="/images/elsa-camper.jpg" alt="Elsa (Klippets Tirhild), visual ambassador of Ballynorsken"></div>
  </div>
</section>

